            "review_title": "Review at Quan An Hong Duc",
            "review_text": "David H\nDymchurch, United Kingdom164 contributions\n0\nCheap --- but by no means cheerful!\nApr 2019 • Couples\nI agree with many of the previous reviews, in that the baseball cap-wearing waitress, when one could eventually gain her attention, actually had a scowl about her face. I tried very hard to be polite and smile at her, but there was no reciprocation.\nI ordered, for my wife and myself, prawn rolls, pork rolls and f/fries. The rolls were extremely greasy. The f/fries were OK, but hey, what's to go wrong with deep-frying frozen chips?\nI wanted to order a second beer, but tired of waiting for her (the waitress) attention, so decided to leave. I knew how much the bill was and I had the correct money, so I found the waitress and put the money in her hand. In case I had made an error, I asked her \"if that was OK\", but she simply counted the money and walked away.\nA previous reviewer mentioned the language problem, yes, there no doubt is, but most nations understand \"OK\", and you don't need to be multilingual to offer a smile, or to understand what it means when someone smiles at you.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten April 22, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-11",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
